How it works

Inputs: a flexible schedule (the decoder7 Schedule.yaml works, and so will a Timefold result), its EnvConfig.yaml, and the old SU_Others. The EnvConfig is needed because the schedule only has worker ids, not names.
Same format: the tool edits the sheet inside the .xlsm zip instead of loading it with openpyxl. openpyxl would drop the macros, buttons, drawings and comments from this file.
Names and colours: a cell that must show a module copies the text and style of a real cell of that module, the same worker’s nearest cell first. So TSMCF21_SU3200_530N03370A_新規 and its colour are never invented.
Cells that leave a module: they become empty, using the sheet’s usual empty-cell style.
Cells that are never overwritten: cells with other tasks or text, red cells, empty grey cells, and cells before --from-date (default today). Blocked cells are listed as CONFLICT in the report.

